<title>SWITZERLAND: CS says no &quot;strategic&quot; Winterthur stake.</title>
<headline>CS says no &quot;strategic&quot; Winterthur stake.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Suisse Group does not hold a strategic stake in insurer Winterthur, which is at the centre of takeover or merger speculation after CS's ally Swiss Reinsurance said it held around five percent of direct insurer.</p>
<p>&quot;We do not have a strategic stake in Winterthur,&quot; CS Group spokesman Andre-Lou Sugar said in an interview with Swiss radio DRS.</p>
<p>Sugar did not elaborate or explain what he meant by &quot;strategic&quot;. He was not immediately available for further comment.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
